<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/017Q">Example <span data-tag="017Q">4.3.4.10</span>.</a> Let $X = \Delta ^{p}$ and $Y = \Delta ^{q}$ be standard simplices. Then the join comparison map $T_{X,Y}: | \Delta ^{p} \star \Delta ^{q} | \rightarrow |\Delta ^{p}| \star | \Delta ^{q} |$ fits into a commutative diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ | \Delta ^{p} \star \Delta ^{q} | \ar [dr]^{ | \rho | } \ar [rr]^{ T_{X,Y} } &amp;  &amp;  | \Delta ^{p} | \star | \Delta ^{q} | \ar [dl]_{ H_{p,q} } \\ &amp;  | \Delta ^{p+1+q} |, &amp;  } \]
</div>
<p> where $\rho : \Delta ^{p} \star \Delta ^{q} \simeq \Delta ^{p+1+q}$ denotes the isomorphism of simplicial sets appearing in Example <a data-tag="0175" href="/tag/0175">4.3.3.14</a> and $H_{p,q}$ is the homeomorphism of Proposition <a data-tag="017N" href="/tag/017N">4.3.4.8</a>. In particular, $T_{X,Y}$ is a homeomorphism. </p>
</article>
